WEBVTT

00:36:57.250 --> 00:37:00.018
AG: OK, then my work is done, good.

00:37:00.042 --> 00:37:02.768
So this goes to a dynamic
that I wanted to talk about,

00:37:02.792 --> 00:37:04.393
being a people pleaser.

00:37:04.417 --> 00:37:07.893
So Esther, is it fair to say
that I am more agreeable,

00:37:07.917 --> 00:37:09.583
more of a people pleaser than you?

00:37:10.750 --> 00:37:12.434
EP: Yes. Yes, yes, yes.

00:37:12.458 --> 00:37:13.768
AG: Why do you say that?

00:37:13.792 --> 00:37:16.434
EP: Because I don't think of myself
as a people pleaser.

00:37:16.458 --> 00:37:17.726
AG: OK.

00:37:17.750 --> 00:37:19.476
I don't think of you as one either.

00:37:19.500 --> 00:37:20.518
(Laughter)

00:37:20.542 --> 00:37:22.601
Which is why I was
so pleasantly surprised.

00:37:22.625 --> 00:37:24.309
EP: But for that we have to define

00:37:24.333 --> 00:37:26.476
what goes in the word
people pleaser, right?

00:37:26.500 --> 00:37:30.393
I mean, this people pleaser,
it's a history of life.